  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-MDA152</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Design and implementation of policies to tackle informality and protect workers improved</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Moldova, 22 percent of workers are engaged in informal employment, with men making up two-thirds of this workforce. Agriculture and construction are the sectors most affected, with informality rates exceeding 60 percent.  

Past formalization policies have been fragmented. Recent ILO analysis highlights that informality stems from multiple factors, including a lack of awareness among employers regarding their obligations, inefficient allocation of labour inspection resources, limited knowledge among informal workers about the benefits of social insurance. 

To address these challenges, the ILO is supporting the development of a diagnostic on undeclared work and non-standard forms of employment, creating a stronger evidence base for policy action. With ILO assistance, the government has approved a National Program to tackle undeclared work through a Ministerial Decree. A targeted campaign is being implemented to increase the number of petitions submitted to the Labour Inspectorate regarding undeclared work, while the introduction of a voucher system for daily workers in agriculture is also being supported to facilitate their transition to formal employment. 

Recognizing their critical role in fostering workplace compliance, the ILO is working with employers&#x2019; and workers&#x2019; organizations to raise awareness of labour law compliance as a means to ensure decent working conditions and enhance productivity. This includes supporting the development and implementation of a communication campaign that informs both workers and employers about their rights and responsibilities, with a focus on occupational safety and health and the risks of undeclared work. The ILO is strengthening workers&#x2019; organizations&#x2019; capacity to effectively prepare and submit complaints to ensure a timely and appropriate response.</narrative>
  </description>
